# Dockerfile.dockerignore, beside the Dockerfile it belongs to.
#
# This service builds from the REPOSITORY root - the only context that
# can see a generated client in a sibling directory - and Docker reads a
# plain .dockerignore only from the context root. A Dockerfile-specific
# ignore-file takes precedence over that and keeps this list with the
# service it describes.
#
# The patterns are therefore repo-wide: ** so they match inside every
# service directory, not just the top level.
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/deploy
**/*.md
